IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`

-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 5, ss 127 to 129: sharing information between the Secretary of
-- State and HMRC (s 127) and the Director of Public Prosecutions (s 128), and the offence of disclosing what the DPP is
-- given (s 129). Layer 1, part wra4. Host Act named in labels: SSA1998 (Social Security Act 1998), whose section 3(1A) s 127(10)
-- amends. Other Acts named in the text: CRCA2005 (Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005), ETA1973 (Employment and
-- Training Act 1973), POCA2002 (Proceeds of Crime Act 2002).
-- The text says who "may" supply and who "must not" disclose. A "may" is read as a power the text grants: where the facts fit it
-- the answer is JUST TRUE, and where they do not the answer is NOTHING, never FALSE, because 127(9) and 128(5) say in terms that
-- the section "does not limit the circumstances in which information may be supplied apart from this section". A "must not"
-- is a bar: where the bar applies the answer is JUST FALSE (the text says no), where its exception applies it is NOTHING.
-- Result convention: JUST FALSE / FALSE = the text says no; NOTHING = not covered (see wra4-ss96-97.l4).

§ `s 127 -- information-sharing between the Secretary of State and HMRC`

DECLARE `s 127 holder of the information` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(1)(a) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    `s 127(1)(b) a person providing services to the Commissioners`
    `s 127(3)(a) the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State`
    `s 127(3)(b) a Northern Ireland Department or a person providing services to a Northern Ireland Department`
    `s 127 some other holder`

DECLARE `s 127 recipient of the information` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(2)(a) the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State`
    `s 127(2)(b) a Northern Ireland Department or a person providing services to a Northern Ireland Department`
    `s 127(2A) the Scottish Ministers`
    `s 127(4) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs or a person providing services to them`
    `s 127 some other recipient`

DECLARE `s 127 purpose of the use` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(2) the purposes of departmental functions`
    `s 127(2A) arrangements made by the Scottish Ministers under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973 by virtue of article 2(1) of the Scotland Act 1998 (Transfer of Functions to the Scottish Ministers etc.) Order 2020`
    `s 127(4) the purposes of HMRC functions`
    `s 127 some other purpose`

-- 127(1): "This subsection applies to information which is held for the purposes of any HMRC functions (a) by the Commissioners,
-- or (b) by a person providing services to them."
-- src:2242 | (1) This subsection applies to information which is held for the purposes of any HMRC functions—
-- src:2243 | (a) by the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs, or
-- src:2244 | (b) by a person providing services to them.
@ref s 127(1) (src:2242-2244)
GIVEN `the information is held for the purposes of any HMRC functions` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held for the purposes of any function of Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs?
      `the holder` IS A `s 127 holder of the information`  @desc Who holds the information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 127(1) subsection (1) applies to the information` MEANS
    IF `the information is held for the purposes of any HMRC functions`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the holder`
          WHEN `s 127(1)(a) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `s 127(1)(b) a person providing services to the Commissioners` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `s 127(3)(a) the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State` THEN FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) by the Commissioners ..., or (b) by a person providing services to them"
          WHEN `s 127(3)(b) a Northern Ireland Department or a person providing services to a Northern Ireland Department` THEN FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) by the Commissioners ..., or (b) by a person providing services to them"
          WHEN `s 127 some other holder` THEN FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) by the Commissioners ..., or (b) by a person providing services to them"
         )
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "information which is held for the purposes of any HMRC functions"

-- 127(2): information to which (1) applies may be supplied (a) to the Secretary of State or a person providing services to
-- the Secretary of State, or (b) to a Northern Ireland Department or a person providing services to one, for use for the
-- purposes of departmental functions.
-- src:2245 | (2) Information to which subsection (1) applies may be supplied—
-- src:2246 | (a) to the Secretary of State, or to a person providing services to the Secretary of State, or
-- src:2247 | (b) to a Northern Ireland Department, or to a person providing services to a Northern Ireland Department,
-- src:2248 | for use for the purposes of departmental functions.
@ref s 127(2) (src:2245-2248)
GIVEN `subsection (1) applies to the information` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held for the purposes of a function of Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs, by them or by a person providing services to them?
      `the recipient` IS A `s 127 recipient of the information`  @desc To whom would the information be supplied?
      `the purpose` IS A `s 127 purpose of the use`  @desc For what would the information be used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(2) information held for HMRC functions may be supplied` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1) applies to the information`
       AND `the purpose` EQUALS `s 127(2) the purposes of departmental functions`
       AND ((`the recipient` EQUALS `s 127(2)(a) the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State`)
            OR (`the recipient` EQUALS `s 127(2)(b) a Northern Ireland Department or a person providing services to a Northern Ireland Department`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may be supplied" to these recipients for this use; 127(9) says the section does not limit other supply

-- 127(2A): such information may be supplied to the Scottish Ministers for use in connection with arrangements made by them
-- under section 2 of ETA1973 by virtue of article 2(1) of the 2020 Order.
-- src:2249 | (2A) Information to which subsection (1) applies may be supplied to the Scottish Ministers for use in connection with any arrangements made by them under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973 by virtue of article 2(1) of the Scotland Act 1998 (Transfer of Functions to the Scottish Ministers etc.) Order 2020.
@ref s 127(2A) (src:2249-2249)
GIVEN `subsection (1) applies to the information` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held for the purposes of a function of Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs, by them or by a person providing services to them?
      `the recipient` IS A `s 127 recipient of the information`  @desc To whom would the information be supplied?
      `the purpose` IS A `s 127 purpose of the use`  @desc For what would the information be used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(2A) information held for HMRC functions may be supplied to the Scottish Ministers` MEANS
    IF `subsection (1) applies to the information`
       AND `the recipient` EQUALS `s 127(2A) the Scottish Ministers`
       AND `the purpose` EQUALS `s 127(2A) arrangements made by the Scottish Ministers under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973 by virtue of article 2(1) of the Scotland Act 1998 (Transfer of Functions to the Scottish Ministers etc.) Order 2020`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may be supplied to the Scottish Ministers for use in connection with" these arrangements; 127(9) says the section does not limit other supply

-- 127(3): "This subsection applies to information which is held for the purposes of any departmental functions (a) by the
-- Secretary of State, or by a person providing services to the Secretary of State, or (b) by a Northern Ireland Department, or
-- by a person providing services to one."
-- src:2250 | (3) This subsection applies to information which is held for the purposes of any departmental functions—
-- src:2251 | (a) by the Secretary of State, or by a person providing services to the Secretary of State, or
-- src:2252 | (b) by a Northern Ireland Department, or by a person providing services to a Northern Ireland Department.
@ref s 127(3) (src:2250-2252)
GIVEN `the information is held for the purposes of any departmental functions` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held for the purposes of any departmental function (social security, employment or training, tax credit prosecutions, child support)?
      `the holder` IS A `s 127 holder of the information`  @desc Who holds the information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 127(3) subsection (3) applies to the information` MEANS
    IF `the information is held for the purposes of any departmental functions`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the holder`
          WHEN `s 127(3)(a) the Secretary of State or a person providing services to the Secretary of State` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `s 127(3)(b) a Northern Ireland Department or a person providing services to a Northern Ireland Department` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `s 127(1)(a) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` THEN FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) by the Secretary of State, or by a person providing services to the Secretary of State, or (b) by a Northern Ireland Department, or by a person providing services to one"
          WHEN `s 127(1)(b) a person providing services to the Commissioners` THEN FALSE          -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) by the Secretary of State, or by a person providing services to the Secretary of State, or (b) by a Northern Ireland Department, or by a person providing services to one"
          WHEN `s 127 some other holder` THEN FALSE                                                -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) by the Secretary of State, or by a person providing services to the Secretary of State, or (b) by a Northern Ireland Department, or by a person providing services to one"
         )
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "information which is held for the purposes of any departmental functions"

-- 127(4): information to which (3) applies may be supplied (a) to the Commissioners, or (b) to a person providing services to
-- them, for use for the purposes of HMRC functions.
-- src:2253 | (4) Information to which subsection (3) applies may be supplied—
-- src:2254 | (a) to the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs, or
-- src:2255 | (b) to a person providing services to them,
-- src:2256 | for use for the purposes of HMRC functions.
@ref s 127(4) (src:2253-2256)
GIVEN `subsection (3) applies to the information` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held for the purposes of a departmental function, by the Secretary of State or a Northern Ireland Department or a person providing services to either?
      `the recipient` IS A `s 127 recipient of the information`  @desc To whom would the information be supplied?
      `the purpose` IS A `s 127 purpose of the use`  @desc For what would the information be used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(4) information held for departmental functions may be supplied` MEANS
    IF `subsection (3) applies to the information`
       AND `the recipient` EQUALS `s 127(4) the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs or a person providing services to them`
       AND `the purpose` EQUALS `s 127(4) the purposes of HMRC functions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may be supplied" to these recipients for this use; 127(9) says the section does not limit other supply

-- 127(5): information supplied under this section must not be supplied by the recipient to any other person or body without
-- (a) the authority of the Commissioners (information supplied under (2) or (2A)); (b) the authority of the Secretary of State
-- (information held as in (3)(a) and supplied under (4)); (c) the authority of the relevant Northern Ireland Department
-- (information held as in (3)(b) and supplied under (4)).
DECLARE `s 127(5) how the information came to the recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(5)(a) supplied under subsection (2) or (2A)`
    `s 127(5)(b) held as mentioned in subsection (3)(a) and supplied under subsection (4)`
    `s 127(5)(c) held as mentioned in subsection (3)(b) and supplied under subsection (4)`
    `s 127(5) supplied under this section in some other way`

DECLARE `s 127(5) whose authority is needed` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(5)(a) the authority of the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    `s 127(5)(b) the authority of the Secretary of State`
    `s 127(5)(c) the authority of the relevant Northern Ireland Department`

-- src:2257 | (5) Information supplied under this section must not be supplied by the recipient of the information to any other person or body without—
-- src:2258 | (a) the authority of the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs, in the case of information supplied under subsection (2) or (2A);
-- src:2259 | (b) the authority of the Secretary of State, in the case of information held as mentioned in subsection (3)(a) and supplied under subsection (4);
-- src:2260 | (c) the authority of the relevant Northern Ireland Department, in the case of information held as mentioned in subsection (3)(b) and supplied under subsection (4).
@ref s 127(5) (src:2257-2260)
GIVEN `the way the information came to the recipient` IS A `s 127(5) how the information came to the recipient`  @desc How did the information reach the recipient?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 127(5) whose authority is needed`
`s 127(5) whose authority the recipient needs before supplying the information to another person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way the information came to the recipient`
    WHEN `s 127(5)(a) supplied under subsection (2) or (2A)` THEN JUST `s 127(5)(a) the authority of the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
    WHEN `s 127(5)(b) held as mentioned in subsection (3)(a) and supplied under subsection (4)` THEN JUST `s 127(5)(b) the authority of the Secretary of State`
    WHEN `s 127(5)(c) held as mentioned in subsection (3)(b) and supplied under subsection (4)` THEN JUST `s 127(5)(c) the authority of the relevant Northern Ireland Department`
    WHEN `s 127(5) supplied under this section in some other way` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the authority only for the three routes it lists

@ref s 127(5) (src:2257-2260)
GIVEN `the way the information came to the recipient` IS A `s 127(5) how the information came to the recipient`  @desc How did the information reach the recipient?
      `the recipient has the authority that is needed` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the recipient the authority of the body the subsection names for this information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(5) the recipient may supply the information to another person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way the information came to the recipient`
    WHEN `s 127(5) supplied under this section in some other way` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the authority only for the three routes it lists
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the recipient has the authority that is needed`
        THEN NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "must not be supplied ... without" the authority; having it lifts the bar but the subsection does not itself permit the supply
        ELSE JUST FALSE                                   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be supplied by the recipient of the information to any other person or body without— (a) ... (b) ... (c)"

-- 127(6): where information supplied under this section has been used for the purposes for which it was supplied, it is lawful
-- for it to be used for any purposes for which information held for those purposes could be used.
-- src:2261 | (6) Where information supplied under this section has been used for the purposes for which it was supplied, it is lawful for it to be used for any purposes for which information held for those purposes could be used.
@ref s 127(6) (src:2261-2261)
GIVEN `the information has been used for the purposes for which it was supplied` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the information already been used for the purposes for which it was supplied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(6) it is lawful to use the information for any purposes for which information held for those purposes could be used` MEANS
    IF `the information has been used for the purposes for which it was supplied`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "Where information supplied under this section has been used for the purposes for which it was supplied"

-- 127(7): the defined terms. "departmental functions" means functions relating to social security, employment or training, the
-- investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits, or child support. The raw text shows a repealed "or" and
-- "..." marks where words were omitted.
DECLARE `s 127(7) kind of function` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(7) a function relating to social security`
    `s 127(7) a function relating to employment or training`
    `s 127(7) a function relating to the investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits`
    `s 127(7) a function relating to child support`
    `s 127(7) some other function`

-- src:2263 | “departmental functions” means functions relating to—
-- src:2264 | social security,
-- src:2265 | employment or training, ...
-- src:2266 | the investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits; or
-- src:2267 | child support;
@ref s 127(7) “departmental functions” (src:2263-2267)
GIVEN `the function` IS A `s 127(7) kind of function`  @desc What does the function relate to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 127(7) the function is a departmental function` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the function`
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function relating to social security` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function relating to employment or training` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function relating to the investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function relating to child support` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) some other function` THEN FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“departmental functions” means functions relating to— social security, employment or training, ... the investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits; or child support"

DECLARE `s 127(7) source of a function` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(7) a function for which the Commissioners are responsible by virtue of section 5 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005`
    `s 127(7) a function which relates to a matter listed in Schedule 1 to the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005`
    `s 127(7) a function conferred by or under the Childcare Payments Act 2014`
    `s 127(7) a function conferred by or under section 2 of, or Schedule 2 to, the Savings (Government Contributions) Act 2017`
    `s 127(7) a function from some other source`

-- src:2268 | “HMRC function” means any function—
-- src:2269 | for which the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs are responsible by virtue of section 5 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005, ...
-- src:2270 | which relates to a matter listed in Schedule 1 to that Act , ...
-- src:2271 | which is conferred by or under the Childcare Payments Act 2014; , or
-- src:2272 | which is conferred by or under section 2 of, or Schedule 2 to, the Savings (Government Contributions) Act 2017 (bonuses in respect of savings in Help-to-Save accounts);
@ref s 127(7) “HMRC function” (src:2268-2272)
GIVEN `the function` IS A `s 127(7) source of a function`  @desc Where does the function come from?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 127(7) the function is an HMRC function` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the function`
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function for which the Commissioners are responsible by virtue of section 5 of the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function which relates to a matter listed in Schedule 1 to the Commissioners for Revenue and Customs Act 2005` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function conferred by or under the Childcare Payments Act 2014` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function conferred by or under section 2 of, or Schedule 2 to, the Savings (Government Contributions) Act 2017` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) a function from some other source` THEN FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“HMRC function” means any function— for which the Commissioners ... which relates to ... which is conferred by or under the Childcare Payments Act 2014 ...or which is conferred by or under section 2 of, or Schedule 2 to, the Savings (Government Contributions) Act 2017"

DECLARE `s 127(7) department` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(7) the Department for Communities`
    `s 127(7) the Department of Finance`
    `s 127(7) the Department for the Economy`
    `s 127(7) some other department`

-- src:2273 | “Northern Ireland Department” means any of the following—
-- src:2274 | the Department for Communities;
-- src:2275 | the Department of Finance;
-- src:2276 | the Department for the Economy.
@ref s 127(7) “Northern Ireland Department” (src:2273-2276)
GIVEN `the department` IS A `s 127(7) department`  @desc Which department is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 127(7) the department is a Northern Ireland Department` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the department`
    WHEN `s 127(7) the Department for Communities` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) the Department of Finance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) the Department for the Economy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(7) some other department` THEN FALSE      -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Northern Ireland Department” means any of the following— the Department for Communities; the Department of Finance; the Department for the Economy"

-- 127(8): functions relating to social security include functions relating to (a) statutory payments under SSCBA 4C(11),
-- (b) maternity allowance under SSCBA 35, (c) the Northern Ireland counterpart of (a), (d) maternity allowance under the
-- Northern Ireland counterpart of 35 or 35B. "Includes" does not close the list.
DECLARE `s 127(8) kind of function relating to social security` IS ONE OF
    `s 127(8)(a) statutory payments as defined in section 4C(11) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992`
    `s 127(8)(b) maternity allowance under section 35 of that Act`
    `s 127(8)(c) statutory payments as defined in section 4C(11) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits (Northern Ireland) Act 1992`
    `s 127(8)(d) maternity allowance under section 35 or 35B of that Act`
    `s 127(8) some other function`

-- src:2277 | (8) For the purposes of this section any reference to functions relating to social security includes a reference to functions relating to—
-- src:2278 | (a) statutory payments as defined in section 4C(11) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992;
-- src:2279 | (b) maternity allowance under section 35 of that Act;
-- src:2280 | (c) statutory payments as defined in section 4C(11) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits (Northern Ireland) Act 1992;
-- src:2281 | (d) maternity allowance under section 35 or 35B of that Act.
@ref s 127(8) (src:2277-2281)
GIVEN `the function` IS A `s 127(8) kind of function relating to social security`  @desc What does the function relate to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(8) the function is treated as relating to social security` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the function`
    WHEN `s 127(8)(a) statutory payments as defined in section 4C(11) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(8)(b) maternity allowance under section 35 of that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(8)(c) statutory payments as defined in section 4C(11) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits (Northern Ireland) Act 1992` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(8)(d) maternity allowance under section 35 or 35B of that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 127(8) some other function` THEN NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "any reference to functions relating to social security includes a reference to functions relating to" these four

-- 127(9): the section does not limit the circumstances in which information may be supplied apart from it.
-- src:2282 | (9) This section does not limit the circumstances in which information may be supplied apart from this section.
@ref s 127(9) (src:2282-2282)
GIVEN `the supply is authorised apart from this section` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the supply of the information authorised by some provision other than section 127?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(9) this section does not limit the supply` MEANS
    IF `the supply is authorised apart from this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the subsection protects supply authorised elsewhere; it does not itself authorise any

-- SSA1998 3(1A)(e), inserted: one more purpose for which information may be used under section 3(1A). The words of 3(1A) that
-- lead into its paragraphs are not printed.
-- src:2283 | (10) In section 3 of the Social Security Act 1998 (use of information), in subsection (1A), after paragraph (d) there is inserted—
-- src:2284 | (e) the investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits.
@ref s 127(10) SSA1998 3(1A)(e) (src:2283-2284)
GIVEN `the purpose is the investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the purpose the investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127(10) SSA1998 3(1A)(e) the purpose is within paragraph (e)` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is the investigation or prosecution of offences relating to tax credits`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the opening words of SSA1998 3(1A) and its paragraphs (a) to (d) are not among the sources

§ `s 128 -- information-sharing between the Secretary of State and the Director of Public Prosecutions`

DECLARE `s 128 supplier` IS ONE OF
    `s 128(1) the Secretary of State`
    `s 128(4) a person providing services to the Secretary of State`
    `s 128 some other supplier`

DECLARE `s 128 kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `s 128(1) social security information`
    `s 128(1) child support information`
    `s 128 some other information`

DECLARE `s 128(2) person` IS ONE OF
    `s 128(2)(a) the Director of Public Prosecutions`
    `s 128(2)(b) a person appointed under section 5 of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985`
    `s 128(2) some other person`

DECLARE `s 128(3) purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 128(3)(a) the institution or conduct of criminal proceedings which relate wholly or partly to social security matters or child support`
    `s 128(3)(b) the giving of advice on any matter relating to criminal proceedings, or criminal offences, which relate wholly or partly to social security matters or child support`
    `s 128(3)(c) the exercise in relation to social security matters or child support of functions assigned to the Director of Public Prosecutions under section 3(2)(g) of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985`
    `s 128(3)(d) the exercise of functions of the Director of Public Prosecutions under Part 2, 5 or 8 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`
    `s 128 some other purpose`

-- 128(2): "The persons referred to in subsection (1) are" the DPP and a person appointed under section 5 of the POCA1985. Closed.
-- src:2288 | (2) The persons referred to in subsection (1) are—
-- src:2289 | (a) the Director of Public Prosecutions;
-- src:2290 | (b) a person appointed under section 5 of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985 (conduct of prosecutions on behalf of Crown Prosecution Service).
@ref s 128(2) (src:2288-2290)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `s 128(2) person`  @desc Who is the person the information would be supplied to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 128(2) the person is a person specified in subsection (2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `s 128(2)(a) the Director of Public Prosecutions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128(2)(b) a person appointed under section 5 of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128(2) some other person` THEN FALSE          -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The persons referred to in subsection (1) are— (a) the Director of Public Prosecutions; (b) a person appointed under section 5 of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985"

-- 128(3): "The purposes referred to in subsection (1) are" (a) to (d). Closed.
-- src:2291 | (3) The purposes referred to in subsection (1) are—
-- src:2292 | (a) the institution or conduct of criminal proceedings which relate wholly or partly to social security matters or child support;
-- src:2293 | (b) the giving of advice to any person on any matter relating to criminal proceedings, or criminal offences, which relate wholly or partly to social security matters or child support;
-- src:2294 | (c) the exercise in relation to social security matters or child support of functions assigned to the Director of Public Prosecutions under section 3(2)(g) of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985;
-- src:2295 | (d) the exercise of functions of the Director of Public Prosecutions under Part 2, 5 or 8 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.
@ref s 128(3) (src:2291-2295)
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `s 128(3) purpose`  @desc For what would the information be used?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 128(3) the purpose is a purpose specified in subsection (3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `s 128(3)(a) the institution or conduct of criminal proceedings which relate wholly or partly to social security matters or child support` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128(3)(b) the giving of advice on any matter relating to criminal proceedings, or criminal offences, which relate wholly or partly to social security matters or child support` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128(3)(c) the exercise in relation to social security matters or child support of functions assigned to the Director of Public Prosecutions under section 3(2)(g) of the Prosecution of Offences Act 1985` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128(3)(d) the exercise of functions of the Director of Public Prosecutions under Part 2, 5 or 8 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128 some other purpose` THEN FALSE            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The purposes referred to in subsection (1) are— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ..."

-- 128(1) and (4): the Secretary of State (including a person providing services to the Secretary of State) may supply social
-- security information or child support information to a person in (2) for a purpose in (3). 128(5): the section does not
-- limit the circumstances in which information may be supplied apart from it.
-- src:2287 | (1) The Secretary of State may supply social security information or child support information to a person specified in subsection (2) for use for a purpose specified in subsection (3).
-- src:2296 | (4) The reference in subsection (1) to the Secretary of State includes a person providing services to the Secretary of State.
-- src:2297 | (5) This section does not limit the circumstances in which information may be supplied apart from this section.
@ref s 128(1), (4), (5) (src:2287-2297)
GIVEN `the supplier` IS A `s 128 supplier`  @desc Who would supply the information?
      `the kind of information` IS A `s 128 kind of information`  @desc Is the information social security information or child support information?
      `the person` IS A `s 128(2) person`  @desc Who would the information be supplied to?
      `the purpose` IS A `s 128(3) purpose`  @desc For what would the information be used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 128(1) the Secretary of State may supply the information` MEANS
    IF ((`the supplier` EQUALS `s 128(1) the Secretary of State`) OR (`the supplier` EQUALS `s 128(4) a person providing services to the Secretary of State`))
       AND ((`the kind of information` EQUALS `s 128(1) social security information`) OR (`the kind of information` EQUALS `s 128(1) child support information`))
       AND `s 128(2) the person is a person specified in subsection (2)` `the person`
       AND `s 128(3) the purpose is a purpose specified in subsection (3)` `the purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may supply" these kinds of information to these persons for these purposes; 128(5) says the section does not limit other supply

-- 128(6): the defined terms. "child support information" and "social security information" are information held for the purposes
-- of the Secretary of State's functions relating to child support, or to social security matters; "social security matters" means
-- social security (including the payments and allowances in section 127(8)), tax credits, and schemes under section 2 of ETA1973.
-- src:2299 | “child support information” means information held for the purposes of any of the Secretary of State’s functions relating to child support;
@ref s 128(6) “child support information” (src:2299-2299)
GIVEN `the information is held for the purposes of the Secretary of State's functions relating to child support` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held for the purposes of any of the Secretary of State's functions relating to child support?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 128(6) the information is child support information` MEANS
    IF `the information is held for the purposes of the Secretary of State's functions relating to child support`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“child support information” means information held for the purposes of any of the Secretary of State's functions relating to child support"

DECLARE `s 128(6) kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 128(6) social security, including the payments and allowances referred to in section 127(8)`
    `s 128(6) tax credits`
    `s 128(6) schemes and arrangements under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973`
    `s 128(6) some other matter`

-- src:2301 | “social security matters” means—
-- src:2302 | social security (including the payments and allowances referred to in section 127(8)),
-- src:2303 | tax credits, and
-- src:2304 | schemes and arrangements under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973.
@ref s 128(6) “social security matters” (src:2301-2304)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `s 128(6) kind of matter`  @desc What does the matter relate to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 128(6) the matter is a social security matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 128(6) social security, including the payments and allowances referred to in section 127(8)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128(6) tax credits` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128(6) schemes and arrangements under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 128(6) some other matter` THEN FALSE          -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“social security matters” means— social security (including the payments and allowances referred to in section 127(8)), tax credits, and schemes and arrangements under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973"

-- src:2300 | “social security information” means information held for the purposes of any of the Secretary of State's functions relating to social security matters;
@ref s 128(6) “social security information” (src:2300-2300)
GIVEN `the information is held for the purposes of the Secretary of State's functions relating to social security matters` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information held for the purposes of any of the Secretary of State's functions relating to social security matters?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 128(6) the information is social security information` MEANS
    IF `the information is held for the purposes of the Secretary of State's functions relating to social security matters`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“social security information” means information held for the purposes of any of the Secretary of State's functions relating to social security matters"

§ `s 129 -- unlawful disclosure of information supplied under section 128`

-- 129(1): a person to whom information is supplied under section 128, or an employee or former employee of such a person, may not
-- disclose the information if it relates to a particular person.
-- src:2306 | (1) A person to whom information is supplied under section 128, or an employee or former employee of such a person, may not disclose the information if it relates to a particular person.
@ref s 129(1) (src:2306-2306)
GIVEN `the information was supplied to a person under section 128` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the information supplied to a person under section 128 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012?
      `the discloser is that person, or an employee or former employee of that person` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Are you that person, or an employee or former employee of that person?
      `the information relates to a particular person` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the information relate to a particular person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(1) subsection (1) bars the disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the information was supplied to a person under section 128`
       AND `the discloser is that person, or an employee or former employee of that person`
       AND `the information relates to a particular person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the bar is on a person to whom information is supplied under section 128, or their employee or former employee, about information relating to a particular person; it says nothing of anyone else

-- 129(1)-(4) together: does the bar in (1) apply to this disclosure? JUST FALSE where (2) or (3) says (1) does not apply.
@ref s 129(1) (src:2306-2306)
GIVEN `the bar in subsection (1) applies by its own words` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Does the bar apply on its own words (you hold information supplied under section 128 about a particular person)? Leave out if not known.
      `subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure by virtue of subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Does subsection (2) take the disclosure out of the bar? Leave out if not known.
      `subsection (1) does not apply to the information by virtue of subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Does subsection (3) take the information out of the bar? Leave out if not known.
      `subsection (1) stands unaffected by any other enactment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is the bar free of any other Act or instrument that provides otherwise? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(1) the bar on disclosure applies to the disclosure` MEANS
    IF (`subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure by virtue of subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`subsection (1) does not apply to the information by virtue of subsection (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to" the disclosures in (2) or the information in (3)
    ELSE (IF (`the bar in subsection (1) applies by its own words` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`subsection (1) stands unaffected by any other enactment` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)                                   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a fact the bar turns on is not known, or another enactment may displace it (129(4))

-- 129(2): subsection (1) does not apply to (a) to (i). The kind of disclosure is asked; (b) turns on whether the Director's
-- restriction is contravened.
DECLARE `s 129(2) kind of disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(2)(a) a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it`
    `s 129(2)(b) a disclosure made for the purposes of a function of the Director of Public Prosecutions`
    `s 129(2)(c) a disclosure made to the Secretary of State, or a person providing services to the Secretary of State, for the purposes of the exercise of functions relating to social security matters or child support`
    `s 129(2)(d) a disclosure made for the purposes of a criminal investigation or criminal proceedings, whether or not in the United Kingdom`
    `s 129(2)(e) a disclosure made for the purposes of a function under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 or of an investigation or proceedings outside the United Kingdom which may lead to an external order`
    `s 129(2)(f) a disclosure made to a person exercising public functions of law enforcement for the purposes of the exercise of those functions in civil proceedings`
    `s 129(2)(g) a disclosure which in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions is desirable for the purpose of safeguarding national security`
    `s 129(2)(h) a disclosure made in pursuance of an order of a court`
    `s 129(2)(i) a disclosure made with the consent of each person to whom the information relates`
    `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind`

-- src:2307 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to—
-- src:2308 | (a) a disclosure of a summary or collection of information so framed as not to enable information relating to any particular person to be ascertained from it;
-- src:2309 | (b) a disclosure made for the purposes of a function of the Director of Public Prosecutions, where the disclosure does not contravene any restriction imposed by the Director;
-- src:2310 | (c) a disclosure made to the Secretary of State, or a person providing services to the Secretary of State, for the purposes of the exercise of functions relating to social security matters (within the meaning of section 128) or child support;
-- src:2311 | (d) a disclosure made for the purposes of a criminal investigation or criminal proceedings (whether or not in the United Kingdom);
-- src:2312 | (e) a disclosure made for the purposes of—
-- src:2313 | (i) the exercise of any functions of the prosecutor under Parts 2, 3 and 4 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002;
-- src:2314 | (ii) the exercise of any functions of the Serious Organised Crime Agency under that Act;
-- src:2315 | (iii) the exercise of any functions of the Director of the Serious Fraud Office, the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Scottish Ministers under, or in relation to, Part 5 or 8 of that Act;
-- src:2316 | (iv) investigations or proceedings outside the United Kingdom which have led or may lead to the making of an external order within the meaning of section 447 of that Act;
-- src:2317 | (f) a disclosure made to a person exercising public functions of law enforcement for the purposes of the exercise of those functions in civil proceedings;
-- src:2318 | (g) a disclosure which in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions is desirable for the purpose of safeguarding national security;
-- src:2319 | (h) a disclosure made in pursuance of an order of a court;
-- src:2320 | (i) a disclosure made with the consent of each person to whom the information relates.
@ref s 129(2) (src:2307-2320)
GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A `s 129(2) kind of disclosure`  @desc What kind of disclosure is it?
      `the disclosure contravenes a restriction imposed by the Director of Public Prosecutions` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the disclosure contravene a restriction imposed by the Director of Public Prosecutions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `s 129(2)(b) a disclosure made for the purposes of a function of the Director of Public Prosecutions` THEN
        IF `the disclosure contravenes a restriction imposed by the Director of Public Prosecutions`
        THEN NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): paragraph (b) applies "where the disclosure does not contravene any restriction imposed by the Director"
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 129(2) a disclosure of some other kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): subsection (2) lists the disclosures to which (1) does not apply; for any other the subsection is silent
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 129(3): subsection (1) does not apply to information relating to schemes and arrangements under section 2 of ETA1973.
-- src:2321 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply in relation to information relating to schemes and arrangements under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973.
@ref s 129(3) (src:2321-2321)
GIVEN `the information relates to schemes and arrangements under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the information relate to schemes and arrangements under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the information` MEANS
    IF `the information relates to schemes and arrangements under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the subsection removes this information from (1); for other information it is silent

-- 129(4): subsection (1) is subject to any other Act or to an instrument made under an Act.
-- src:2322 | (4) Subsection (1) is subject to any other Act or to an instrument made under an Act.
@ref s 129(4) (src:2322-2322)
GIVEN `another Act, or an instrument made under an Act, provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does another Act, or an instrument made under an Act, provide otherwise for this disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(4) subsection (1) stands unaffected by any other enactment` MEANS
    IF `another Act, or an instrument made under an Act, provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what the other Act or instrument provides is not among the sources
    ELSE JUST TRUE                                        -- subsection (1) governs as it stands

-- 129(5): a person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence.
-- src:2323 | (5) A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence.
@ref s 129(5) (src:2323-2323)
GIVEN `the bar on disclosure applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Does the bar on disclosure in section 129(1) apply to the disclosure? Leave out if not known.
      `the person made the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Did the person make the disclosure?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person made the disclosure` AND (`the bar on disclosure applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "A person who contravenes subsection (1) commits an offence"; the subsection says nothing of one who does not contravene it

-- 129(6): a defence for a person charged with disclosing, if they prove they reasonably believed (a) the disclosure was lawful
-- or (b) the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public.
-- src:2324 | (6) It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under this section of disclosing information to prove that he or she reasonably believed—
-- src:2325 | (a) that the disclosure was lawful, or
-- src:2326 | (b) that the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public.
@ref s 129(6) (src:2324-2326)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under this section of disclosing information` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Are you charged with an offence under section 129 of disclosing information?
      `the person proves that they reasonably believed the disclosure was lawful` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Can you prove that you reasonably believed the disclosure was lawful?
      `the person proves that they reasonably believed the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Can you prove that you reasonably believed the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(6) the person has a defence` MEANS
    IF `the person is charged with an offence under this section of disclosing information`
       AND (`the person proves that they reasonably believed the disclosure was lawful`
            OR `the person proves that they reasonably believed the information had already and lawfully been made available to the public`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "It is a defence ... to prove that he or she reasonably believed"; the subsection does not say there is no defence otherwise

-- 129(7): liable (a) on conviction on indictment to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine or both, or (b) on
-- summary conviction to imprisonment not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates' court or a fine not exceeding the
-- statutory maximum or both. 129(9): for an offence committed in England and Wales before 2 May 2022 the general limit is read
-- as six months. The text does not give the general limit's figure: it is a name for a figure set elsewhere.
DECLARE `s 129(7) term of imprisonment` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(7)(a) a term of two years`
    `s 129(7)(b) the general limit in a magistrates' court`
    `s 129(9) a term of six months`

DECLARE `s 129(7) limit of a fine` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(7)(a) a fine without a stated limit`
    `s 129(7)(b) the statutory maximum`

DECLARE `s 129(7) punishment` HAS
    `the term of imprisonment not exceeded` IS A `s 129(7) term of imprisonment`
    `the fine not exceeded`                 IS A `s 129(7) limit of a fine`

DECLARE `s 129(7) mode of conviction` IS ONE OF
    `s 129(7)(a) conviction on indictment`
    `s 129(7)(b) summary conviction`

-- src:2327 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:2328 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine or both, or
-- src:2329 | (b) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or both.
@ref s 129(7) (src:2327-2329)
GIVEN `the mode of conviction` IS A `s 129(7) mode of conviction`  @desc Would you be convicted on indictment or summarily?
GIVETH A `s 129(7) punishment`
`s 129(7) the greatest punishment for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the mode of conviction`
    WHEN `s 129(7)(a) conviction on indictment` THEN
        `s 129(7) punishment` WITH
            `the term of imprisonment not exceeded` IS `s 129(7)(a) a term of two years`,
            `the fine not exceeded` IS `s 129(7)(a) a fine without a stated limit`
    WHEN `s 129(7)(b) summary conviction` THEN
        `s 129(7) punishment` WITH
            `the term of imprisonment not exceeded` IS `s 129(7)(b) the general limit in a magistrates' court`,
            `the fine not exceeded` IS `s 129(7)(b) the statutory maximum`

-- src:2331 | (9) In relation to an offence under this section committed before 2 May 2022, the reference in subsection (7)(b) to the general limit in a magistrates’ court shall have effect as if it were a reference to six months.
@ref s 129(9) (src:2331-2331)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 129(7) term of imprisonment`  @desc Which term applies to you?
      `the offence was committed in England and Wales before 2 May 2022` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the offence committed in England and Wales before 2 May 2022?
GIVETH A `s 129(7) term of imprisonment`
`s 129(9) the term as read for an offence committed before 2 May 2022` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `s 129(7)(b) the general limit in a magistrates' court` THEN
        IF `the offence was committed in England and Wales before 2 May 2022`
        THEN `s 129(9) a term of six months`
        ELSE `s 129(7)(b) the general limit in a magistrates' court`
    WHEN `s 129(7)(a) a term of two years` THEN `s 129(7)(a) a term of two years`
    WHEN `s 129(9) a term of six months` THEN `s 129(9) a term of six months`

-- 129(8): a prosecution may be instituted only with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions.
-- src:2330 | (8) A prosecution for an offence under this section may be instituted only with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions.
@ref s 129(8) (src:2330-2330)
GIVEN `the Director of Public Prosecutions consents to the prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the Director of Public Prosecutions consented to the prosecution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 129(8) a prosecution may be instituted` MEANS
    IF `the Director of Public Prosecutions consents to the prosecution`
    THEN NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "may be instituted only with the consent"; consent is necessary, not sufficient
    ELSE JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A prosecution for an offence under this section may be instituted only with the consent of the Director of Public Prosecutions"
